    <bpmn:task id="task_btxk8ebi" name="Remove dogfighting" dai:notes="Scope change on 2026-11-11: removed all combat, so Baron is now free flight only (take off, explore, land on any strip).&#10;Removed: src/combat (weapons.ts, ai.ts); the Dogfight mission and the hangar&#39;s Mission and Enemy pilots selectors; the enemy livery; the fire input (Space / click / RT), ammo, gun heat and the spec.ammo setting; the padlock camera (C now switches between chase and cockpit); gun muzzle and ground-hit effects; enemy markers, the lead diamond, the aim reticle and the ammo/heat HUD panel; gun/hit/ouch sounds, positional enemy engines and the audio listener; and kills and accuracy in the debrief and best records.&#10;Kept: the damage model from prop strikes and wing scrapes, with the damage silhouette in its own HUD panel and the low-health red edge; bail out (X), where the empty plane spirals down; and the mouse-stick cursor. The twin guns stay on the biplane mesh as decoration.&#10;Medals now depend only on the landing grade: A/A+ gold, B silver, any landing bronze. Best records are keyed free:&#60;seed&#62;, and older saved settings have mission and difficulty removed when they load. steer.ts now keeps only bankAngle.&#10;Docs: README and the in-game controls list were updated. design.dai and plan.dai still describe dogfighting.&#10;Verified: tsc clean, vitest 11/11, vite build OK (577 KB main, 155 KB gzip). Not played in the browser." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_wh0abcn5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_31dm82bc</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_wh0abcn5" sourceRef="task_9gbykx6r" targetRef="task_btxk8ebi" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_9by84gvy" name="Loadout &#38; spec composer" dai:notes="plane/loadout.ts: Loadout type + options (3 styles, 8 paints, 3 engines, 3 wheels), AIRFRAMES (base spec, taildragger/tricycle gear, prop mount, jet exhausts, crash points), ENGINE_DEFS (thrust-to-weight, thrust lapse speed, spool rate, mass), WHEEL_DEFS (spring/damper, friction, crash speed, grip per surface), composeSpec(), gearFor(), stallSpeed(), loadoutStats() for the hangar bars, sanitize/parse/print, localStorage &#39;baron.loadout.v1&#39; + ?plane=style.paint.engine.wheels. flight.ts: Gear (contact + crash points) passed to stepFlight/groundAttitude/restHeight (default = the original biplane), spoolRate, nose wheel, &#39;tail&#39; strike points (scrape), per-wheel surface grip via Env.surfaceAt. Deviation from design numbers: jet engine T/W 0.55 with thrust falling to 0 at 200 m/s (keeps jet top speed ≈ 133 m/s / 478 km/h), jet airframe mass 2500 kg, wing 22 m². composeSpec(default) === DEFAULT_SPEC, so the original biplane flies exactly as before. Matrix test (27 flight combos × paint-independent): all take off and land; worst ground roll Jet+Prop+Soft 504 m (limit 630), worst landing roll Jet+Jet+Soft 599 m. Test pilot needed AoA-targeted rotation, stall protection and bounce handling." dai:agentStatus="done" dai:planRef="task_dm9i0pir">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_31dm82bc</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_lz6vxihb</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_31dm82bc" sourceRef="task_btxk8ebi" targetRef="task_9by84gvy" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_gz4xh2hq" name="Airframe, engine &#38; wheel meshes" dai:notes="plane/planeMesh.ts replaces biplaneMesh.ts: PlaneVisual(loadout) with builders for Biplane (original, guns removed), Turboprop (low wing, bubble canopy, tricycle gear) and Jet (nose cone, swept wings, side intakes, swept fin, nozzle). Engine attachments: 2-blade wooden prop, 4-blade steel prop + spinner + exhaust stacks, jet (nose intake + side exhaust pipes on prop airframes) with additive flame cones scaled by RPM. Wheels sized per tyre choice (r 0.30 / 0.36 / 0.48). 8 paints via liveryFor(); Sky and Snow get a dark stripe. Swept, tapered fins via finGeo(). Prop radius clamped per airframe for ground clearance. ~1.2k triangles. Checked in Chrome via canvas captures (the screenshot tool timed out on every page): all three styles, jet-on-biplane and prop-on-jet render correctly. Deviation: a paint change rebuilds the mesh instead of recolouring in place (a few ms, not noticeable)." dai:agentStatus="done" dai:planRef="task_0fp4papg">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_lz6vxihb</bpmn:incoming>
